  "generatedAt": "2026-10-03T02:43:17.440Z",
  "title": "osf review: multi-agent PR review pipeline",
  "summary": "Adds a whole review subsystem to osf: a lens catalogue (20 shipped lenses plus repository overrides), a reviewer roster built from the `[agents]` table in `osf.toml`, per-reviewer headless runs of coding agents (codex, claude, opencode, omp, dsh) inside a clean copy of the change, quote verification of every finding against the real files, a deterministic reducer that turns answers into a per-lens and whole-review verdict, and a GitHub Actions workflow that builds osf from the base branch, runs each reviewer in its own job with only its own provider key, and posts the decision from a final job that alone holds the code-host token. Alongside it, suppression markers gain rule ownership so a checker only reports unused markers it could have judged, and `osf scan --no-suppress` is added for CI.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
